<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Applying permutations to elect club leadership committees</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>(a)</b> A club has \({@pn1@}\) members. In how many ways can they elect a President, Secretary, and Treasurer?</p>
<p>Number of ways = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><b>(b)</b> A different club has \({@pn2@}\) members. In how many ways can they elect just a Chairperson and a Vice-Chairperson?</p>
<p>Number of ways = [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part (a):</b><br>
Because President, Secretary, and Treasurer are \(3\) distinct positions, the order of selection matters. We use the permutation formula \(\displaystyle {}_nP_r = \frac{n!}{(n - r)!}\) with \(n = {@pn1@}\) and \(r = 3\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_{{@pn1@}}P_{3} = \frac{{@pn1@}!}{({@pn1@} - 3)!} = \frac{{@pn1@}!}{{@pn1_m3@}!}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">Expand \({@pn1@}!\) until it matches \({@pn1_m3@}!\) and cancel the common factor:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_{{@pn1@}}P_{3} = \frac{{@pn1@} \times {@pn1_m1@} \times {@pn1_m2@} \times {@pn1_m3@}!}{{@pn1_m3@}!} = {@pn1@} \times {@pn1_m1@} \times {@pn1_m2@} = {@pn1_step1@} \times {@pn1_m2@} = {@ta1@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ {}_{{@pn1@}}P_{3} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>

<p><b>Part (b):</b><br>
Because Chairperson and Vice-Chairperson are \(2\) distinct positions, order matters. Use \(\displaystyle {}_nP_r = \frac{n!}{(n - r)!}\) with \(n = {@pn2@}\) and \(r = 2\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_{{@pn2@}}P_{2} = \frac{{@pn2@}!}{({@pn2@} - 2)!} = \frac{{@pn2@}!}{{@pn2_m2@}!}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">Expand \({@pn2@}!\) until it matches \({@pn2_m2@}!\) and cancel the common factor:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_{{@pn2@}}P_{2} = \frac{{@pn2@} \times {@pn2_m1@} \times {@pn2_m2@}!}{{@pn2_m2@}!} = {@pn2@} \times {@pn2_m1@} = {@ta2@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ {}_{{@pn2@}}P_{2} = {@ta2@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
